# The scenes of the slow-and-failing-dependencies deck, in order. Each "## Scene N: title" is one slide, spoken with item N of
# slow-and-failing-dependencies.narration.md. Each line under a heading puts one thing on the slide:
#   note "<text>"         a line of text
#   show <file> ...       a code panel: <from> <to> or /pattern/, then a label; --mark and --zoom mark lines
#   run_live "<command>"  a live run, played from its cast in slow-and-failing-dependencies.outputs/
#   callout "<text>"      a boxed sentence saying what a result means

## Scene 1: step 1, the version catalogue
note "Step 1: add WireMock to the version catalogue."
show libs.versions.toml "/wiremock/" gradle/libs.versions.toml

## Scene 2: step 2, the test dependency
note "Step 2: add it as a test dependency of the lesson."
show lessons/slow-and-failing-dependencies/example/build.gradle.kts "/^dependencies/" "lesson build file" --zoom 10

## Scene 3: the code under test
note "The code under test: today's stock client. *No timeout*, and a failed connection is thrown on."
show TodaysStockClient 26 37 "today's stock client" --zoom 29-32

## Scene 4: the weak test
note "The *weak* tests: a stand-in supplier answers at once, with stock or with 503."
show StockAnswerTest 33 44 "the weak tests" --zoom 41-43

## Scene 5: the strong tests
note "The *strong* tests: WireMock makes the supplier slow, or breaks the connection."
show SupplierFaultTest 43 56 "the strong tests" --zoom 45-47

## Scene 6: the supplier fails
note "Run the tests against today's code:"
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:slow-and-failing-dependencies:test -Pcode=today"
callout "A slow supplier kept the shop waiting, and a broken connection became an exception, not an answer."

## Scene 7: the fixed client
note "The client with a connect and a read timeout, and a clear fallback:"
show StockClient 24 43 "the fixed client" --zoom 25,33
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:slow-and-failing-dependencies:test"
callout "Too slow, reset, empty or broken: the shop answers supplier unavailable within a second."
